{"name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"What exists today beyond this repo — is there a backend, task data, or user accounts anywhere?","header":"What exists","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Just this repo","description":"The static index.html is the entire app. No tasks, users, storage, or server exist yet anywhere."},{"label":"Backend exists elsewhere","description":"There's a real API/database with tasks and users; this page is (or will be) a client for it."},{"label":"Prototype / demo only","description":"Nothing real behind it and none planned — browser-local fake data is fine for this exercise."}]}]}}
{"name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Who are the \"users\" — multiple real people sharing tasks, or just you?","header":"User model","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Single user (Recommended)","description":"Just me. Notifications = reminders + a 'what changed' view, all browser-local. No server or accounts."},{"label":"Multiple real people","description":"Tasks are shared/assigned across people. Needs a server, accounts, and sync — build tasks and identity first, notifications after."},{"label":"Single user now, multi later","description":"Build for one user but keep the door open. I'd flag where that costs us and what would still need redoing."}]}]}}
{"name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"What should actually trigger a notification?","header":"Triggers","multiSelect":true,"options":[{"label":"Due soon / overdue (Recommended)","description":"Clock-driven reminders on tasks with due dates. The only thing that changes without you acting."},{"label":"Activity log of changes","description":"Scrollable history of edits/completions. Needs a stored event log; informational rather than interrupting."},{"label":"Changes from other tabs","description":"Notify when the same app open in another tab modifies a task. Needs cross-tab sync handling."},{"label":"Recurring task rollover","description":"A repeating task becoming active again generates a notification."}]}]}}
{"name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"How should a due/overdue reminder reach you?","header":"Delivery","multiSelect":true,"options":[{"label":"In-app badge + panel (Recommended)","description":"App renders a count and a list of due/overdue tasks. No permissions, works everywhere, easy to test."},{"label":"Plus OS desktop toasts","description":"Browser Notification API on top of the in-app layer. Reaches you on other tabs; needs a permission prompt and a blocked-fallback."},{"label":"Must work with app closed","description":"Requires a server and web push — contradicts serverless. Pick this and we revisit the architecture now."}]}]}}
{"name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Should reminders be dismissible, and if so how?","header":"Reminder state","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Snooze field on task (Recommended)","description":"Derived list, plus a remindAfter timestamp per task. Snoozing hides it temporarily. One source of truth."},{"label":"Purely derived, no dismiss","description":"Panel is a pure filter over tasks. Simplest possible; overdue tasks nag until completed or rescheduled."},{"label":"Stored notification records","description":"Each reminder is a persisted object with seen/dismissed state. Most flexible, most sync bugs."}]}]}}
